  "notes": "Composed of {再|さい} (again) + {選|せん} (election/selection). A standard political term frequently seen in news about elections.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {再選|さいせん}される: to be re-elected\n- {再選|さいせん}を{目指|めざ}す: to aim for re-election\n- {再選|さいせん}を{果|は}たす: to achieve re-election\n- {再選|さいせん}{出馬|しゅつば}: running for re-election\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {当選|とうせん}: winning an election — used for both first-time and subsequent wins\n- {落選|らくせん}: losing an election — the opposite outcome\n- {再任|さいにん}: reappointment — for appointed rather than elected positions",
